The generated snippets follow the WebMCP imperative surface. That
specification is not vendored. It is pinned, as of 2026-10-19, to:

  https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp
  commit f14762e63607bf96592b1a7a6392cd2b047b8209
  (2026-10-16, "Editorial: sync explainers with spec (#350)")

The same surface is described by the Chrome WebMCP imperative API
documentation, last updated 2026-10-16:

  https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api

Polyfill behavior was checked against @mcp-b/webmcp-polyfill 6.0.3
(MIT, Alex Nahas / MCP-B), which vendors upstream revision
6bf6c57bbaf3d1173d7737cfb79572632d9b7871. That package's source is
not copied. The in-repo modelContext implementation is original and
covers the subset the offline demo needs: registerTool, getTools,
executeTool, toolchange, and AbortSignal unregistration on
document.modelContext. It does not install the deprecated
navigator.modelContext alias.

provideContext() and clearContext() were removed from the spec in
https://github.com/webmachinelearning/webmcp/pull/132 (merged
2026-03-05) and are not emitted.

The image token estimate reimplements the published OpenAI vision
tile count (rescale to fit 2048, shortest side 768, then
85 + 170 tokens per 512px tile). No OpenAI source is included.
Text tokens use the common ceil(chars / 4) approximation. Both are
estimates for the offline race, not a provider bill.
